{"data": [{"author_id": "2062520217230880768", "created_at": "2026-10-27T06:27:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114967325141278757"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/AshZQhNv9i", "end": 248, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/mayaislam_ai/status/2114967325141278757/video/1", "media_key": "13_2114967317973184512", "start": 225, "url": "https://t.co/AshZQhNv9i"}]}, "id": "2114967325141278757", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 47, "impression_count": 6282, "like_count": 75, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 27}, "text": "𝗢𝗽𝗲𝗻𝗔𝗜'𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗲𝘁𝗲 𝗔𝗜 𝗔𝗴𝗲𝗻𝘁 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝗰𝗸: 𝗠𝗼𝗱𝗲𝗹𝘀, 𝗧𝗼𝗼𝗹𝘀, 𝗠𝗲𝗺𝗼𝗿𝘆 &amp; 𝗗𝗲𝗽𝗹𝗼𝘆𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁\n\nOpenAI's GPT-6 Astra launch has intensified the AGI debate.\n\nNVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang declared, \"AGI has arrived,\" while OpenAI President Greg Brockman https://t.co/AshZQhNv9i", "url": "https://x.com/mayaislam_ai/status/2114967325141278757"}, {"author_id": "266259493", "created_at": "2026-10-28T09:12:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115370989781684609"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/cognition/stat…", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/cognition/status/2115132488775524793", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/lIcFBE0zW4"}]}, "id": "2115370989781684609", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 204, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115132488775524793", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Would a maintainer actually merge this PR? That's the question Cognition's new FrontierCode 2.0 asks every model, and the honest answer right now is mostly no.\n\nThe benchmark structure is deliberate. Tasks are written by real open source maintainers, not by Cognition's own https://t.co/lIcFBE0zW4", "url": "https://x.com/stretchcloud/status/2115370989781684609"}, {"author_id": "1709245282553053185", "created_at": "2026-10-28T17:11:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115491603876036651"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/OfficialLoganK…", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/OfficialLoganK/status/2115489284404940898", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.co/IrMZkL7GIM"}]}, "id": "2115491603876036651", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 396, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115489284404940898", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "🚨Gemini 4 carbon dropped just now. \n\n&gt;tops AA index(#1) \n&gt;tops SWE\n&gt;tops terminal bench\n&gt;tops automation bench\n&gt;better benchamrk score than opus\n&gt;better benchmark score than astra\n&gt;better benchmark score than argon\n\nGoogle just cooked with this one. https://t.co/IrMZkL7GIM", "url": "https://x.com/adityaa_behera/status/2115491603876036651"}, {"author_id": "64268528", "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:06:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115460234017743046"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/simonw/status/…", "end": 152, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/simonw/status/2115444742595260551", "start": 129, "url": "https://t.co/nToc23yovN"}]}, "id": "2115460234017743046", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115444742595260551", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The benchmark that matters was never SWE-bench. It's \"would a bored 12-year-old play this twice.\" Looks like we just crossed it. https://t.co/nToc23yovN", "url": "https://x.com/Pilgrimnow/status/2115460234017743046"}, {"author_id": "2115165741531971585", "created_at": "2026-10-28T17:57:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115503231405051939"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/simonw/status/…", "end": 159, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/simonw/status/2115444742595260551", "start": 136, "url": "https://t.co/FhAgHUqYAJ"}]}, "id": "2115503231405051939", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115444742595260551", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "fun is the one eval nobody can benchmark-max\n\nif opus is actually clearing it, thats a bigger result than any swe-bench chart this year https://t.co/FhAgHUqYAJ", "url": "https://x.com/StephenBuildsAI/status/2115503231405051939"}, {"author_id": "1308990535357652993", "created_at": "2026-10-28T14:01:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115443879512346722"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/owoKPelLmO", "end": 312, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/kumawataman13/status/2115443879512346722/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115443870335209473", "start": 289, "url": "https://t.co/owoKPelLmO"}]}, "id": "2115443879512346722", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 93, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Next week, Anthropic is dropping its best model, Fable 5.5 \n\nLeak inside Fable 5.5:\n\n1. Release date: first week of Nov \n\n2. Capacity:\n&gt; 1M context window \n&gt; Output Token Limit is 128k\n&gt; Adaptive Reasoning\n\n3. Benchmark:\n&gt; SWE-bench Pro benchmark; it probably beats OpenAI 6.1 https://t.co/owoKPelLmO", "url": "https://x.com/kumawataman13/status/2115443879512346722"}, {"author_id": "2963648527", "created_at": "2026-10-27T03:49:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114927512560255022"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/KnJRqdDAyw", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/imhaoyi/status/2114927512560255022/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114927502812749824", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/KnJRqdDAyw"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/KnJRqdDAyw", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/imhaoyi/status/2114927512560255022/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114927502837886976", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/KnJRqdDAyw"}]}, "id": "2114927512560255022", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 41, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Nanbeige, the model lab inside BOSS Zhipin, just open-sourced Nanbeige4.3-33B. A 33B dense model, 512K context, Apache 2.0. It wins 17 of the 20 benchmarks they picked.\n\nThe wins aren't close. Terminal-Bench 2.1: 80.9 against Qwen3.8-27B at 73.0. DeepSWE: 65.5 against 42.5. https://t.co/KnJRqdDAyw", "url": "https://x.com/imhaoyi/status/2114927512560255022"}, {"author_id": "47344769", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:09:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115506314516586668"], "id": "2115506314516586668", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "SWE-bench Verified hit 96% about two years after launch. GLUE lasted as long; MMLU lasted four. Each benchmark generation has a shorter shelf life, not because tasks get easier but because labs optimize against the metric. Harder successors show the same pattern.", "url": "https://x.com/18dew/status/2115506314516586668"}, {"author_id": "1859338255780446208", "created_at": "2026-10-28T13:18:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115433101518115095"], "id": "2115433101518115095", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 148, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "diffuspace dropped clover-35b overnight. open weight diffusion llm, 3b active, built on qwen3.6-35b-a3b\n\n680 tok/s on a single card and 73.6 on swe-bench verified are both their own numbers so grain of salt\n\nthe speed is the part i care about tbh. an agent loop making 40 tool", "url": "https://x.com/RaghavMehtaM1/status/2115433101518115095"}, {"author_id": "3097139297", "created_at": "2026-10-26T22:12:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114842517380190477"], "id": "2114842517380190477", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Nanbeige has released Nanbeige4.3-33B, an open-weight model aimed at coding and multi-step agent work.\n\nThe model card lists a 512K context window and an Apache 2.0 license. The team also plans to use this 33B model as a teacher for smaller agents.\n\nIts benchmark table reports", "url": "https://x.com/Layerquill/status/2114842517380190477"}, {"author_id": "2013613489798160388", "created_at": "2026-10-28T17:09:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115491072684302527"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/FtzBYvsraG", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AGTPinsights/status/2115491072684302527/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115491052694175744", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/FtzBYvsraG"}, {"display_url": "x.com/FireworksAI_HQ…", "end": 325, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/FireworksAI_HQ/status/2115474253055455296", "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/5JigjEkspu"}]}, "id": "2115491072684302527", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 241, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115474253055455296", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Fireworks AI just added 31 new partners to its Specialized Intelligence Index today. Here's what you need to know.\n\nFireworks says it is working to build the largest collection of private and public practitioner evals. The Index lets teams compare open, closed, and specialized https://t.co/FtzBYvsraG https://t.co/5JigjEkspu", "url": "https://x.com/AGTPinsights/status/2115491072684302527"}, {"author_id": "1562843426185674755", "created_at": "2026-10-27T04:03:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114931081027760633"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/oluwaphilemon1…", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/oluwaphilemon1/status/2114912451963896284", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/XrGdsVhbc2"}]}, "id": "2114931081027760633", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 581, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114912451963896284", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "You don’t necessarily need a closed-source model to build a capable coding agent.\n\nNanbeige4.3-33B has arrived under the Apache 2.0 license, and its published benchmark results put it ahead of Qwen3.8-27B on two agent-focused evaluations.\n\nNanbeige4.3-33B vs Qwen3.8-27B\n\nDeepSWE: https://t.co/XrGdsVhbc2", "url": "https://x.com/Oluwaphilemon1/status/2114931081027760633"}, {"author_id": "2029271146445848578", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:20:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115206964485787767"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 32, "id": "240008974", "start": 20, "username": "GregKamradt"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/IVIWYBmU7c", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2115206964485787767/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115206910886748160", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/IVIWYBmU7c"}, {"display_url": "x.com/17739351601926…", "end": 326, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/1773935160192647168/status/2095597602545025138", "start": 303, "url": "https://t.co/A0EWXxTJJl"}]}, "id": "2115206964485787767", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 6599, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2095597602545025138", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "ARC Prize President @GregKamradt explains why Astra scoring 99% on ARC-AGI-3 doesn't mean AI has achieved AGI:\n\n\"Astra was very good at ARC-AGI-3 using one of OpenAI’s harnesses. It got something like 99%, so more or less it saturated the benchmark.\"\n\n\"The reason why is because https://t.co/IVIWYBmU7c https://t.co/A0EWXxTJJl", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2115206964485787767"}, {"author_id": "1998136947701927936", "created_at": "2026-10-27T20:15:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115175603682914687"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/DdZHSZMyyh", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/VibeCoderOfek/status/2115175603682914687/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115175596506423296", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/DdZHSZMyyh"}]}, "id": "2115175603682914687", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 95, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"Max reasoning effort\" isn't the safe default. It's often the expensive way to lose tasks you'd already solved.\n\nTested: 8 models (GPT-5.6 luna/terra/sol, Claude Sonnet 5, GLM-5.2, Kimi K3, DeepSeek V4 Flash, Inkling) on AIME, GPQA, Terminal-Bench, SWE-Bench Pro.\n\nWhat they https://t.co/DdZHSZMyyh", "url": "https://x.com/VibeCoderOfek/status/2115175603682914687"}, {"author_id": "1703499086928687104", "created_at": "2026-10-28T17:37:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115498267509424551"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/GoogleDeepMind…", "end": 315, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2115489356437651654", "start": 292, "url": "https://t.co/KwxK5SYbqK"}]}, "id": "2115498267509424551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115489356437651654", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "google just dropped gemini 4 carbon\n\n&gt; it beats opus and astra in quite literally every single benchmark\n&gt; #1 on AA and specifically terminal bench and SWE-sweep both of which are very unsaturated and not very susceptible to benchmaxxing\n&gt;not available to normal users yet.\n&gt;best https://t.co/KwxK5SYbqK", "url": "https://x.com/be_arsh/status/2115498267509424551"}, {"author_id": "979737336", "created_at": "2026-10-27T15:20:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115101393811824826"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/nkKlLo65lB", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/cutetoxicguy/status/2115101393811824826/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115101109966561281", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/nkKlLo65lB"}]}, "id": "2115101393811824826", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 158, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚀 Mirendil just unveiled Fern, a new AI model with a massive 10 MILLION token context window, enough to process roughly 500,000 lines of code at once!\n\nAnd unlike models that simply advertise enormous context windows, Fern has demonstrated the ability to retrieve information https://t.co/nkKlLo65lB", "url": "https://x.com/cutetoxicguy/status/2115101393811824826"}, {"author_id": "1627503387276193792", "created_at": "2026-10-27T03:02:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114915684052558226"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/LuoYaoshen/sta…", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/LuoYaoshen/status/2114682847512739915", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/O6JNYMj7PV"}]}, "id": "2114915684052558226", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 276, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114682847512739915", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Last night before falling asleep, and again while running by the lake this morning, my mind kept returning to the two tasks that failed on Harbor / Terminal-Bench yesterday.\n\nI’m not satisfied with merely getting results close to mini-SWE-agent on some partial checks. I keep https://t.co/O6JNYMj7PV", "url": "https://x.com/LuoYaoshen/status/2114915684052558226"}, {"author_id": "1759191266581966848", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:00:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114824453724975544"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/6s9qCA2E7p", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MaryamMiradi/status/2114824453724975544/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114824123239006208", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/6s9qCA2E7p"}]}, "id": "2114824453724975544", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 1121, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🛠️🧭 I went down the Agentic AI research rabbit hole.\n\nIf you want to master Agentic AI Engineering, there is much more to understand than prompts, LLMs, and agent frameworks.\n\nYou need to understand how agents reason, plan, use tools, remember, collaborate, retrieve knowledge, https://t.co/6s9qCA2E7p", "url": "https://x.com/MaryamMiradi/status/2114824453724975544"}, {"author_id": "2003012593494241280", "created_at": "2026-10-27T16:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115118830293062041"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/hexvt6WunY", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/designwithdnkys/status/2115118830293062041/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115075594736295936", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/hexvt6WunY"}]}, "id": "2115118830293062041", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 40, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Breakdown an AI feature that guesses can only be scored, never proven. three habits we would copy:\n\n1. keep a fixed test set. write 20 real user requests, mark the right tool for each, run them, count the passes. that percentage is your reliability number. it's called an eval (a https://t.co/hexvt6WunY", "url": "https://x.com/designwithdnkys/status/2115118830293062041"}, {"author_id": "1696905219538313216", "created_at": "2026-10-28T12:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115420820906410444"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/c6gDqsKDtV", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/OwnYourCompute/status/2115420820906410444/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114577085813399552", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/c6gDqsKDtV"}]}, "id": "2115420820906410444", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Damn, a new Apache 2.0 open model just dropped and it's going straight at agentic coding.\n\nNanbeige4.3-33B: 33B parameters, 512K context, built for coding agents and tool use. It's the \"teacher\" for a smaller 3B distill they've announced.\n\nLab-reported scores vs Qwen3.8-27B (from https://t.co/c6gDqsKDtV", "url": "https://x.com/OwnYourCompute/status/2115420820906410444"}, {"author_id": "2029271146445848578", "created_at": "2026-10-27T23:15:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115220830854774918"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 32, "id": "240008974", "start": 20, "username": "GregKamradt"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/yJpSvyciHI", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2115220830854774918/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115220796935380993", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/yJpSvyciHI"}]}, "id": "2115220830854774918", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 6214, "like_count": 27, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "ARC Prize President @GregKamradt explains why AI researchers could be among the last jobs automated:\n\n\"AI is very good at executing what you want it to do. It’s not very good at coming up with ideas. It’s not very good at coming up with hypotheses.\"\n\n\"We tried to make ARC-AGI-3 https://t.co/yJpSvyciHI", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2115220830854774918"}, {"author_id": "1966807787133886464", "created_at": "2026-10-28T17:23:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115494646012948581"], "id": "2115494646012948581", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Can a small model get better at a hard reasoning benchmark without touching its weights?\nRecursive Self-Improvement for ARC-AGI-3: Hill-Climbing to 78.95 RHAE with Haiku 5.5 and ASSAY\n\nThe loop:\nI wrapped a human-in-the-loop RSI loop around ASSAY (my open-source reasoning", "url": "https://x.com/freddie_spirit/status/2115494646012948581"}, {"author_id": "1339962951843778562", "created_at": "2026-10-27T14:32:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115089322651320821"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Mh3Zyn0Iy8", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ChenBuildsAI/status/2115089322651320821/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115089196104945664", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/Mh3Zyn0Iy8"}]}, "id": "2115089322651320821", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 57, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ARC Prize ran OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra through ARC-AGI-3 twice and published both numbers: 62.7% on its standard, provider-neutral harness, and 99.9% on OpenAI's own Provider Adapter. Same model. The difference is the harness — what the model is allowed to carry between requests. On https://t.co/Mh3Zyn0Iy8", "url": "https://x.com/ChenBuildsAI/status/2115089322651320821"}, {"author_id": "1110487793933778945", "created_at": "2026-10-27T09:22:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115011226883563574", "2115011342495310116"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/2TI0V4QXnW", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/HyperAI_News/status/2115011226883563574/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115005341507420160", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.co/2TI0V4QXnW"}]}, "id": "2115011226883563574", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Nanbeige4.3-33B vs Qwen3.8-27B\n\nNanbeige4.3-33B vs Qwen3.8-27B\nMeasured on a single A100 80GB, both native BF16, no 4-bit or 8-bit quantization.\n\n= = =\n\nMODEL\nReleased Oct 24, 2026 by Nanbeige LLM Lab\nApache 2.0, 33.1B dense, 524,288-token context, text only\n\nBENCHMARKS https://t.co/2TI0V4QXnW", "url": "https://x.com/HyperAI_News/status/2115011226883563574"}, {"author_id": "1110487793933778945", "created_at": "2026-10-27T09:22:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115011226883563574"